1559 0 obj
  << /ActualText (High in the frozen reaches of the world\054 where icy winds scour the bare rock and severe winter deters most civilized life\054 the Frost Elves thrive\056 These solitary people have made their sanctuary in some of the most unforgiving climates on Pliiara\054 establishing their primary cities and settlements throughout the frozen expanses of Tundwine\056 While smaller\054 scattered populations occasionally brave the bleak conditions of the Barren\054 they almost never venture into Angoran\054 holding a deep seated aversion to the creatures that inhabit those lands\056\n\nTowering over most of their kin\054 Frost Elves stand an average of six feet tall\054 making them one of the tallest elven subraces\056 Their long\054 distinctive ears often droop slightly along the sides of their head unless held close or tucked beneath warm coverings\056 To mirror their bitter surroundings\054 their skin displays a striking\054 dark shade of grayish blue that almost perfectly matches the color of their hair\056\n\nAlthough centuries of living in extreme climates have made them hardy\054 they remain mortal creatures who still feel the bite of a severe blizzard\056 To survive the harshest storms\054 they have developed a unique mystical gift\072 an innate magic that allows them to generate living flame for warmth at a moment\047s notice\056 Highly reclusive and fiercely independent\054 Frost Elves rarely invite outsiders into their homes\054 viewing other races as little more than an unwelcome nuisance\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 1560 0 R
     /Pg 950 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

