1586 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Standing noticeably taller than average human beings\054 the Elves of Pliiara possess a graceful and slender physique that is strikingly accentuated by long\054 tapered ears\056 Their eyes are wide and almond shaped\054 filled with large and vibrantly colored pupils that immediately draw the attention of outsiders\056 It is a frequent mistake among other species to assume that their thin limbs indicate weakness or feebleness\054 as an elf can wield surprising physical power when pushed to action\056\n\nAmong all the known inhabitants of Pliiara\054 the Elves remain among the longest living creatures on the map\056 This vast longevity shapes every single aspect of their culture\054 philosophy\054 and everyday existence\056 Because an individual elf can expect to remain active within the same locale for many centuries\054 short term solutions simply do not work for them\056 By sheer necessity\054 they must learn to build and maintain deeply sustainable lifestyles\056 These enduring habits are most easily achieved when they choose to work in harmony with the natural world\054 rather than attempting to force nature to bend to their collective will\056\n\nTheir deep rooted connection to the wilderness is not driven purely by practical needs or simple survival strategies\056 Elves naturally find themselves far more in tune with raw nature and spiritual energies than short lived species ever could be\056 Their long lifespans give them ample time to cultivate deep connections to mystical abilities\054 allowing them to sense subtle shifts in the land that others completely miss\056 As a generally patient and docile people\054 they spend their vast lifespans seeking a genuine\054 profound understanding of their world and the invisible forces that drive it\056\n\nPerhaps the most fascinating aspect of these people is the way their physical forms respond to their surroundings\056 The body of an elf slowly changes over time\054 gradually taking on a physical representation of their mental\054 emotional\054 and spiritual states\056 Furthermore\054 those who dwell within a specific region for an extended period find themselves physically adapting to match the local terrain\056 This shift is most noticeable in their coloration\054 which subtly alters to mirror the surrounding landscape\056\n\nBecause of this unique biological trait\054 the overall coloration across the entire elf population varies wildly\054 proving far more diverse than human populations ever display\056 Yet within any single community\054 the local inhabitants often look remarkably similar to one another because they draw from the exact same environment\056 Forest dwelling communities\054 for instance\054 frequently exhibit rich variations of green\054 deep brown\054 and warm tan across their hair\054 eyes\054 and skin tones\056 Through this seamless blend of physical adaptation\054 deep spiritual awareness\054 and timeless patience\054 the Elves remain intimately tied to the living heartbeat of Pliiara\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 1587 0 R
     /Pg 1552 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1587 0 obj
  << /K [ 1586 0 R ]
     /P 1590 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1552 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1588 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Ability Scores\056 Your Dexteriry Score increases by 2\nAge\056 Although elves reach physical maturity around the same age as humans\054 the elven understanding of adulthood reaches far beyond mere biological growth\056 To an elf\054 true maturity encompasses extensive worldly experience and spiritual growth\056 An elf typically claims adulthood and chooses an adult name around 100 years of age\054 and individuals can live to be 750 years old\056\nAlignment\056 Elves value freedom\054 variety\054 and personal self expression\054 which leads them to lean strongly toward the gentler aspects of chaos\056 They cherish and protect the freedom of others just as fiercely as their own\056 Driven by compassion and respect for life\054 they are far more often good than not\056\nSize\056 Elves range from under 5 feet to over 6 feet tall\054 maintaining remarkably slender builds throughout their lives\056 Your size is Medium\056\nSpeed\056 Your base walking speed is 30 feet\056\nDarkvision\056 Accustomed to twilight forests and the night sky\054 you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions\056 You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light\054 and in darkness as if it were dim light\056 You cannot discern color in darkness\054 only shades of gray\056\nKeen Senses\056 You have natural proficiency in the Perception skill\056\nFey Ancestry\056 Your heritage grants you resistance to certain magical effects\056 You have advantage on saving throws against being charmed\054 and magic cannot put you to sleep\056\nTrance\056 Elves do not need to sleep in the way humans do\056 Instead\054 they meditate deeply for 4 hours a day\054 remaining fully semiconscious during this period\056 The Common word for this mental state is a trance\056 While meditating\054 you experience a unique form of dreaming\073 these dreams are actually structured mental exercises that have become reflexive through long years of practice\056 After resting in this manner\054 you gain the exact same benefits that a human receives from 8 hours of deep sleep\056\nLanguages\056 You can speak\054 read\054 and write Common and Elvish\056 Elvish is a remarkably fluid language\054 renowned for its subtle intonations\054 delicate cadence\054 and intricate grammatical structures\056 Elven literature is vast\054 rich\054 and deeply varied\054 spanning centuries of recorded history\054 philosophy\054 and myth\056 Beyond their written works\054 their songs and poems are famous across all lands\054 celebrated for their haunting beauty and emotional depth\056 Bards of many different ancestral backgrounds routinely dedicate years to learning the language simply to add authentic Elvish ballads and poetic epics to their performing repertoires\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 1589 0 R
     /Pg 1552 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

